1
00:00:02,055 --> 00:00:04,425
Last time, in 2001:

2
00:00:04,445 --> 00:00:05,121
A Space Odyssey,

3
00:00:05,141 --> 00:00:07,540
a black monolith on the Moon sent

4
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:09,065
a signal to Jupiter.

5
00:00:09,085 --> 00:00:10,805
The ship Discovery followed it,

6
00:00:10,825 --> 00:00:11,680
and its computer,

7
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:13,725
HAL, turned on the crew.

8
00:00:13,745 --> 00:00:15,775
Dave Bowman shut HAL down,

9
00:00:15,795 --> 00:00:17,575
flew into a monolith at Jupiter,

10
00:00:17,595 --> 00:00:19,620
and became the Star Child.

11
00:00:19,705 --> 00:00:21,370
Discovery was left behind,

12
00:00:21,390 --> 00:00:23,020
empty and silent.

13
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:24,325
Now, part two:

14
00:00:24,345 --> 00:00:27,525
2010: The Year We Make Contact.

15
00:00:27,545 --> 00:00:28,819
Spoilers ahead!

16
00:00:29,529 --> 00:00:31,284
It's nine years later.

17
00:00:31,304 --> 00:00:33,184
Heywood Floyd lost his job over

18
00:00:33,204 --> 00:00:35,009
the Discovery disaster.

19
00:00:35,029 --> 00:00:36,559
Now there's a deadline:

20
00:00:36,579 --> 00:00:38,599
Discovery's orbit is sinking,

21
00:00:38,619 --> 00:00:39,349
and it will crash

22
00:00:39,369 --> 00:00:41,274
into Jupiter's moon Io before

23
00:00:41,294 --> 00:00:43,449
an American ship can get there.

24
00:00:43,469 --> 00:00:45,799
The Soviet ship Leonov can.

25
00:00:45,819 --> 00:00:47,849
So, even with Cold War tension

26
00:00:47,869 --> 00:00:50,074
on Earth, three Americans fly

27
00:00:50,094 --> 00:00:51,574
with the Russian crew:

28
00:00:51,594 --> 00:00:54,009
Floyd, the engineer Walter Curnow,

29
00:00:54,029 --> 00:00:57,048
and HAL's creator, Dr. Chandra.

30
00:00:57,784 --> 00:01:00,189
Near Jupiter, the Leonov's instruments pick up

31
00:01:00,209 --> 00:01:02,839
chlorophyll on the icy moon Europa.

32
00:01:02,859 --> 00:01:04,364
That could mean life.

33
00:01:04,384 --> 00:01:05,629
They send a probe to look,

34
00:01:05,649 --> 00:01:08,029
but a burst of energy destroys it.

35
00:01:08,049 --> 00:01:11,129
Floyd thinks it's a warning: stay away.

36
00:01:11,149 --> 00:01:12,829
Then the Leonov slows down

37
00:01:12,849 --> 00:01:13,944
the risky way,

38
00:01:13,964 --> 00:01:17,119
by skimming through Jupiter's clouds to brake.

39
00:01:17,139 --> 00:01:18,744
The ship glows red hot,

40
00:01:18,764 --> 00:01:20,440
but the crew survives.

41
00:01:21,126 --> 00:01:23,731
They find Discovery tumbling over Io,

42
00:01:23,751 --> 00:01:26,206
covered in yellow sulfur dust.

43
00:01:26,226 --> 00:01:28,756
Curnow and a young cosmonaut named Max

44
00:01:28,776 --> 00:01:31,426
make a scary spacewalk across to it.

45
00:01:31,451 --> 00:01:33,216
Curnow hates being outside,

46
00:01:33,236 --> 00:01:34,541
but they make it.

47
00:01:34,561 --> 00:01:37,206
Inside, it's dark and freezing.

48
00:01:37,226 --> 00:01:38,506
Piece by piece,

49
00:01:38,526 --> 00:01:40,866
Curnow brings the ship's power back,

50
00:01:40,886 --> 00:01:42,996
and Discovery comes back to life.

51
00:01:43,736 --> 00:01:45,966
Nearby floats the giant monolith

52
00:01:45,986 --> 00:01:48,811
that Dave flew into nine years before.

53
00:01:48,836 --> 00:01:51,066
The crew calls it Big Brother.

54
00:01:51,086 --> 00:01:52,691
Max takes a pod out to get

55
00:01:52,711 --> 00:01:53,986
a close look.

56
00:01:54,101 --> 00:01:55,291
As he reaches the surface,

57
00:01:55,311 --> 00:01:57,431
a burst of energy shoots out,

58
00:01:57,451 --> 00:01:59,606
and his pod is destroyed.

59
00:01:59,626 --> 00:02:01,106
Max is gone.

60
00:02:01,126 --> 00:02:03,081
Whatever the monolith is doing,

61
00:02:03,101 --> 00:02:04,665
it doesn't want visitors.

62
00:02:05,379 --> 00:02:08,024
Chandra carefully wakes HAL back up,

63
00:02:08,044 --> 00:02:10,724
and finally finds out what went wrong.

64
00:02:10,744 --> 00:02:13,024
HAL had secret orders:

65
00:02:13,044 --> 00:02:16,294
keep the real mission hidden from Dave and Frank.

66
00:02:16,369 --> 00:02:18,124
But HAL was built to tell

67
00:02:18,144 --> 00:02:20,414
the truth, and couldn't do both.

68
00:02:20,434 --> 00:02:21,764
Lying broke him.

69
00:02:21,784 --> 00:02:23,189
So it wasn't evil.

70
00:02:23,209 --> 00:02:24,589
It was the humans who gave him

71
00:02:24,609 --> 00:02:26,526
that impossible choice.

72
00:02:27,190 --> 00:02:28,170
Back on Earth,

73
00:02:28,190 --> 00:02:29,645
things get worse.

74
00:02:29,665 --> 00:02:31,970
America and the Soviet Union clash,

75
00:02:31,990 --> 00:02:34,495
and the two countries move toward war.

76
00:02:34,515 --> 00:02:35,820
Orders come in:

77
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:38,045
the Americans must leave the Leonov

78
00:02:38,065 --> 00:02:39,870
and stay on Discovery.

79
00:02:39,890 --> 00:02:40,795
The two crews,

80
00:02:40,815 --> 00:02:42,220
who had become friends,

81
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:44,520
now float side by side,

82
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:48,643
separated by politics almost a billion kilometers from home.

83
00:02:49,364 --> 00:02:51,919
Then someone unexpected appears.

84
00:02:51,939 --> 00:02:53,763
Dave Bowman, now a being without

85
00:02:53,783 --> 00:02:56,069
a body, comes back to Earth.

86
00:02:56,089 --> 00:02:57,044
He says goodbye

87
00:02:57,064 --> 00:02:58,269
to his former wife through

88
00:02:58,289 --> 00:02:59,669
her TV screen,

89
00:02:59,689 --> 00:03:00,794
and he visits his mother

90
00:03:00,814 --> 00:03:01,844
in the hospital,

91
00:03:01,864 --> 00:03:03,419
one last time.

92
00:03:03,439 --> 00:03:06,019
Then Dave appears to Floyd on Discovery,

93
00:03:06,039 --> 00:03:07,244
with a message:

94
00:03:07,264 --> 00:03:09,694
something wonderful is going to happen.

95
00:03:09,714 --> 00:03:12,236
You must leave Jupiter within two days.

96
00:03:12,939 --> 00:03:14,219
Two days is too soon

97
00:03:14,239 --> 00:03:15,739
to fly home.

98
00:03:15,814 --> 00:03:17,494
But then a black spot appears

99
00:03:17,514 --> 00:03:20,019
on Jupiter, and it's growing fast.

100
00:03:20,039 --> 00:03:21,844
HAL looks closer:

101
00:03:21,864 --> 00:03:25,024
it's millions of monoliths, multiplying.

102
00:03:25,044 --> 00:03:27,519
The crews work together on a plan.

103
00:03:27,634 --> 00:03:30,214
Discovery's fuel will push the Leonov out,

104
00:03:30,234 --> 00:03:31,864
like a booster rocket.

105
00:03:31,884 --> 00:03:33,114
That means Discovery,

106
00:03:33,134 --> 00:03:35,080
and HAL, will be left behind.

107
00:03:35,843 --> 00:03:38,398
Floyd fears HAL might break again,

108
00:03:38,418 --> 00:03:40,143
if he learns the truth.

109
00:03:40,218 --> 00:03:42,793
But Chandra tells HAL everything,

110
00:03:42,813 --> 00:03:44,193
and HAL agrees

111
00:03:44,213 --> 00:03:46,343
to help them escape anyway.

112
00:03:46,363 --> 00:03:47,968
As the countdown runs,

113
00:03:47,988 --> 00:03:49,693
HAL asks Chandra,

114
00:03:49,713 --> 00:03:50,943
will I dream?

115
00:03:50,963 --> 00:03:53,093
Chandra answers, I don't know.

116
00:03:53,113 --> 00:03:55,968
Then a familiar voice speaks to HAL.

117
00:03:55,988 --> 00:03:57,029
It's Dave.

118
00:03:57,765 --> 00:04:00,295
Dave asks HAL to send one message

119
00:04:00,315 --> 00:04:02,415
to Earth, again and again.

120
00:04:02,510 --> 00:04:05,470
All these worlds are yours, except Europa.

121
00:04:05,490 --> 00:04:07,170
Attempt no landing there.

122
00:04:07,190 --> 00:04:08,445
Use them together.

123
00:04:08,465 --> 00:04:09,970
Use them in peace.

124
00:04:09,990 --> 00:04:12,220
HAL says he's afraid.

125
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:13,120
Dave tells him,

126
00:04:13,140 --> 00:04:15,060
don't be, we'll be together.

127
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:17,285
Then the monoliths collapse Jupiter,

128
00:04:17,305 --> 00:04:20,212
and Discovery and HAL are swallowed up.

129
00:04:20,964 --> 00:04:22,494
Jupiter ignites.

130
00:04:22,514 --> 00:04:24,089
It's now a small star,

131
00:04:24,109 --> 00:04:25,464
and Earth has two suns

132
00:04:25,484 --> 00:04:26,714
in the sky.

133
00:04:26,734 --> 00:04:28,694
Seeing it, and hearing the message,

134
00:04:28,714 --> 00:04:32,469
America and the Soviet Union step back from war.

135
00:04:32,489 --> 00:04:34,319
Far away, under the new sun,

136
00:04:34,339 --> 00:04:36,694
the ice of Europa begins to melt,

137
00:04:36,714 --> 00:04:38,669
and life starts to grow.

138
00:04:38,689 --> 00:04:40,757
That's the year we made contact.

